# Lab site

A service on `calculus` is not reachable on the lab domain until every item below is in the same change. Caddy alone does not create the DNS name. The domain comes from `inputs.nix-private.lab.domain` (see existing `site` helpers in `caddy.nix` / `pihole.nix` / `homepage.nix`).

1. Listen on `127.0.0.1` and an unused port. Check `modules/nixos/caddy.nix` and `modules/nixos/gatus.nix` before picking one.
2. Add a `virtualHosts` entry in `modules/nixos/caddy.nix` with `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:<port>` and `${tls}` (follow the existing `site "name"` pattern).
3. Add a `cnameRecords` entry in `modules/nixos/pihole.nix` pointing at `lab.calculusHostname`.
4. Add a link in `modules/nixos/homepage.nix`.
5. Add a loopback check in `modules/nixos/gatus.nix`.

Leave `hosts/AGENTS.md` alone. Record a calculus note only when the service breaks this loopback pattern.

qBittorrent is the exception: it runs inside the Mullvad namespace, so Caddy uses `reverse_proxy 192.168.15.1:8090`.
